; (staying <flap>) overrides the leading-element convention. Same incenter
; rabbit ear as flatten-rabbit-ear-toward-a.bel, but the leading pair is
; SWAPPED to (--eb .b)(--ea .a) — an order whose <180 arc is a small folding
; sector, not the stayer, so the bare convention seats a flap off the paper
; (see flatten-order-load-bearing.bel). Naming the stationary strip material
; with (staying .d) restores the correct stayer regardless of element order;
; {toward .a} then picks the a-side mirror, exactly as the convention-ordered
; toward-a case does. `.t = --ear * --ab` errors unless the a-side ear was
; picked (the c-side ear line is parallel to --ab).

paper square

mark (through .a .c) as --diag
mark (map --ab onto --diag) as --ea
mark (map --ab onto --bc) as --eb
mark (map --bc onto --diag) as --ec

flatten (--eb & .b) (--ea & .a) (--ec & .c) (staying .d) (toward .a) as --ear
.t = --ear * --ab

; assert --ear is mountain
